  "_id": "tg-stranger",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "thy seed shall be a stranger, Gen. 15:13. land wherein thou art a stranger, Gen. 17:8. I am a stranger and a sojourner, Gen. 23:4 (Ps. 39:12). Jacob dwelt … wherein his father was a stranger, Gen. 37:1. a stranger in a strange land, Ex. 2:22. Canaan … wherein they were strangers, Ex. 6:4. passover … no stranger eat thereof, Ex. 12:43. not do any work, thou … nor thy stranger, Ex. 20:10 (Mosiah 13:18). neither vex a stranger, Ex. 22:21. stranger that dwelleth with you shall be … as one born among you, Lev. 19:34. ye are strangers and sojourners, Lev. 25:23 (1 Chr. 29:15). one ordinance, both for the stranger, and for him that was born in the land, Num. 9:14. Love ye therefore the stranger: for ye were strangers, Deut. 10:19. Unto a stranger thou mayest lend upon usury, Deut. 23:20. shalt not pervert the judgment of the stranger, Deut. 24:17. Solomon numbered all the strangers, 2 Chr. 2:17. cleansed I them from all strangers, Neh. 13:30. I am a stranger in the earth, Ps. 119:19. strangers shall be joined with them, Isa. 14:1 (2 Ne. 24:1). sons of strangers shall build up thy walls, Isa. 60:10. shall ye serve strangers, Jer. 5:19. dealt by oppression with the stranger, Ezek. 22:7. Strangers have devoured his strength, Hosea 7:9. Jerusalem … no strangers pass through her, Joel 3:17. witness against … those … that turn aside the stranger, Mal. 3:5 (3 Ne. 24:5).",
