      "text": "I was a stranger, and ye took me in, Matt. 25:35. potter’s field, to bury strangers in, Matt. 27:7. they know not the voice of strangers, John 10:5. dwelt as strangers in the land of Egypt, Acts 13:17. ye were … strangers from the covenants, Eph. 2:12. ye are no more strangers and foreigners, Eph. 2:19. confessed that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth, Heb. 11:13 (D&C 45:13). Be not forgetful to entertain strangers, Heb. 13:2. Peter … to the strangers scattered, 1 Pet. 1:1. I beseech you as strangers, 1 Pet. 2:11. whatsoever thou doest to the brethren, and to strangers, 3 Jn. 1:5.",
